From: C2000MAX maintainers <noreply@example.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 20:45:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: mediatek: document external uplink HQoS restriction

C2000MAX uses an HNAT external device such as eth2 for its cellular
uplink and sends that traffic through the PPD-reserved queue.  A normal
per-device HQoS QID must not be forced onto this external ping-pong path:
doing so collapses throughput for every client while the mode is enabled.

Keep HQOS_FLAG restricted to a real HNAT WAN endpoint.  The C2000MAX EQoS
service enables HQoS for the LAN/downlink direction only and uses selective
tc/IFB shaping for limited uploads. Unrelated uploads remain on HNAT.
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_hnat/hnat.h | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_hnat/hnat.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_hnat/hnat.h
@@ -1476,6 +1476,10 @@ enum FoeIpAct {
 #define PINGPONG_EXT_ID GENMASK(5, 0)
 #define PINGPONG_MAPE_TOKEN 0x01
 
+/* External USB/cellular uploads use the PPD queue and must stay out of the
+ * ordinary uplink HQoS QID path. Downstream LAN HQoS remains valid.
+ */
+
 #define HQOS_FLAG(dev, skb, qid)				\
 	((IS_HQOS_UL_MODE && IS_WAN(dev)) ||			\
 	 (IS_HQOS_DL_MODE && IS_LAN_GRP(dev)) ||		\
 	 (IS_PPPQ_MODE && (IS_PPPQ_PATH(dev, skb) ||		\
 			   qid >= MAX_PPPQ_QUEUE_NUM)))
